		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Lawrence]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:42:31 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">http://itgonglun.wordpress.com/?p=6160</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[@pianobaby120: 這句「Be a human first, a musician second,  [&#8230;]]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><a href="https://www.threads.com/@pianobaby120/post/Dfnm49UDrHX?xmt=AQG07Um5Z5nCTo6_b-oxUR73K27GvmMOp3457D0lm0bC5UncnC3I6v1MzGOxGc6a6wUD0BiR&amp;slof=1">@pianobaby120</a>:</p>
<blockquote><p>這句「Be a human first, a musician second, and then your instrument」（先做人，其次才是音樂家）是王羽佳的美國鋼琴老師加里·格拉夫曼（Gary Graffman）向她提出。</p>
<p>希望她真的理解呢句說話不只是口號，而是一個真正音樂家的態度。</p></blockquote>
<p>指的是近日王羽佳在香港的演出臨時減少曲目，主辦方退款的<a href="https://www.hk01.com/社會新聞/60409761/鋼琴家王羽佳香港演出突取消曲目-主辦方指藝術考量-將全額退款">事件</a>。</p>
<p>中國的古典音樂愛好者可能更熟悉傅雷的<a href="https://www.sohu.com/a/220331088_780786">版本</a>：「做人第一，其次才是做藝術家，再其次才是做音樂家，最後才是做鋼琴家。」和 Graffman 的相比，我更喜歡這個說法。<a href="https://blog.yitianshijie.net/2023/12/11/a-certain-kind-of-genealogy/#:~:text=%E9%81%8E%E5%8E%BB%E5%BB%BF%E4%BA%94%E5%B9%B4%EF%BC%8C%E5%92%8C%E5%85%92%E7%AB%A5%E8%88%87%E9%83%A8%E5%88%86%E6%88%90%E5%B9%B4%E4%BA%BA%E4%B8%80%E8%B5%B7%E5%B7%A5%E4%BD%9C%E7%9A%84%E7%B6%93%E9%A9%97%E5%91%8A%E8%A8%B4%E6%88%91%EF%BC%8C%E6%8A%80%E8%A1%93%E5%B0%8D%E6%96%BC%E6%95%99%E8%82%B2%E7%94%A8%E8%99%95%E4%B8%8D%E5%A4%A7%E3%80%82%E5%9C%A8%E6%95%99%E5%AE%A4%E8%A3%8F%E6%94%BE%E4%B8%80%E5%8F%B0%E9%8B%BC%E7%90%B4%E4%B8%A6%E4%B8%8D%E8%83%BD%E5%9F%B9%E9%A4%8A%E5%87%BA%E9%9F%B3%E6%A8%82%E5%AE%B6%E3%80%82%E9%9F%B3%E6%A8%82%E4%B8%8D%E5%9C%A8%E9%8B%BC%E7%90%B4%E8%A3%8F%E3%80%82%E9%8B%BC%E7%90%B4%E5%85%85%E5%85%B6%E9%87%8F%E5%8F%AA%E8%83%BD%E6%94%BE%E5%A4%A7%E4%B8%80%E5%80%8B%E4%BA%BA%E6%9C%AC%E6%9C%89%E7%9A%84%E9%9F%B3%E6%A8%82%E8%A1%9D%E5%8B%95%E3%80%82%E5%B0%87%E6%8A%80%E8%A1%93%E9%81%8B%E7%94%A8%E6%96%BC%E4%BA%BA%E6%99%82%E5%BF%85%E9%A0%88%E6%85%8E%E4%B9%8B%E5%8F%88%E6%85%8E%E3%80%82%0A%0A%E4%B8%8D%E9%81%8E%EF%BC%8C%E6%9C%89%E7%9A%84%E6%A8%82%E5%99%A8%E5%A4%96%E8%A1%A8%E9%96%83%E4%BA%AE%EF%BC%8C%E5%BE%88%E5%90%B8%E5%BC%95%E4%BA%BA%EF%BC%8C%E4%BE%8B%E5%A6%82%E3%80%8C%E4%B8%83%E5%8D%81%E5%85%AD%E6%8A%8A%E9%95%B7%E8%99%9F%E3%80%8D%E9%80%99%E7%A8%AE%E6%9D%B1%E8%A5%BF%E3%80%82%E6%88%91%E5%80%91%E6%87%89%E8%A9%B2%E5%88%A9%E7%94%A8%E9%80%99%E7%A8%AE%E5%90%B8%E5%BC%95%E5%8A%9B%E3%80%82%E4%BD%86%E8%A6%81%E5%81%9A%E5%88%B0%E9%80%99%E9%BB%9E%EF%BC%8C%E5%B0%B1%E5%BF%85%E9%A0%88%E8%A8%AD%E8%A8%88%E4%B8%80%E5%A5%97%E5%AE%8C%E5%85%A8%E4%B8%8D%E4%BE%9D%E8%B3%B4%E6%96%BC%E6%8A%80%E8%A1%93%E4%B9%9F%E8%83%BD%E6%88%90%E7%AB%8B%E7%9A%84%E8%AA%B2%E7%A8%8B%E3%80%82%E9%80%99%E5%A5%97%E8%AA%B2%E7%A8%8B%E5%BF%85%E9%A0%88%E4%BD%9C%E7%94%A8%E6%96%BC%E5%AD%B8%E7%94%9F%E7%9A%84%E8%BA%AB%E9%AB%94%E8%88%87%E5%BF%83%E9%9D%88%EF%BC%8C%E8%A6%81%E5%83%8F%E6%98%AF%E8%87%AA%E5%B8%B6%E7%89%B9%E6%AE%8A%E5%AA%92%E4%BB%8B%E9%82%A3%E6%A8%A3%E5%8E%BB%E8%A8%AD%E8%A8%88%E5%AE%83%E3%80%82%E5%AE%8C%E6%88%90%E4%B9%8B%E5%BE%8C%EF%BC%8C%E5%8F%AF%E4%BB%A5%E5%8A%A0%E5%85%A5%E6%8A%80%E8%A1%93%E4%BE%86%E6%94%BE%E5%A4%A7%E6%9F%90%E4%BA%9B%E5%8B%95%E4%BD%9C%E3%80%82%0A%0A%E6%88%91%E6%83%B3%E8%AA%AA%E7%9A%84%E6%98%AF%E8%A6%81%E6%8F%90%E5%8D%87%E6%A8%82%E6%84%9F%E4%B8%A6%E4%B8%8D%E9%9C%80%E8%A6%81%E6%A8%82%E5%99%A8%EF%BC%8C%E9%96%8B%E5%8F%A3%E6%AD%8C%E5%94%B1%E5%B0%B1%E5%A5%BD%E3%80%82">樂器不是必須的</a>——#AlanSaidIt30YearsAgo。</p>
<p>我不知道王羽佳引述 Graffman 這句話有多準確，但 be a human 恐怕和如今中華人民共和國說的「做人」並不相同。它是指像一個有缺陷的人一樣好好生活和精進。妳先得是一個活生生的人，然後才是音樂家。會臨時取消音樂會的音樂家就是一個活生生的人。</p>
<p>（<a href="https://yitianshijie.vercel.app/2026/11/12/6160">點此</a>讀豎排版）</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
